ge and performance.\n- **Success Criteria:** Reduce maximum transmission power to 43.0dBm.\n\n### **Violation 6: Predicted Maximum Transmission Power**\n\n- **Corrective Action:** Consider antenna-level power optimization instead of full BS power reduction.\n- **Configuration Change:** Implement load-based dynamic energy optimization.\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor impact on network coverage and performance.\n- **Success Criteria:** Ensure predicted maximum transmission power remains below 43.0dBm.\n\n### **Violation 7: Current Autonomous Vehicle Network Slice**\n\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for critical services.\n- **Configuration Change:** Enable low latency mode and reduce processing delay.\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor throughput degradation during latency optimization.\n- **Success Criteria:** Achieve autonomous vehicle network slice latency of 5.0ms or below.\n\n### **Violation 8: Predicted Autonomous Vehicle Network Slice**\n\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for critical services.\n- **Configuration Change:** Enable low latency mode and reduce processing delay.\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor throughput degradation during latency optimization.\n- **Success Criteria:** Ensure predicted autonomous vehicle network slice latency remains below 5.0ms.\n\n### **Violation 9: Current URLLC Services General**\n\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for critical services.\n- **Configuration Change:** Enable low latency mode and reduce processing delay.\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor throughput degradation during latency optimization.\n- **Success Criteria:** Achieve URLLC services latency of 1.0ms or below.\n\n### **Violation 10: Predicted URLLC Services General**\n\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for critical services.\n- **Configuration Change:** Enable low latency mode and reduce processing delay.\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor throughput degradation during latency optimization.\n- **Success Criteria:** Ensure predicted URLLC services latency remains below 1.0ms.\n\n---\n\nBy following this detailed healing plan, you can systematically address each critical violation in the 5G network optimization, implement necessary corrective actions, make configuration changes to meet policy requirements, mitigate risks effectively, and define success criteria for each healing step. This practical approach will help optimize the network performance and ensure compliance with policies.",
