 Predicted URLLC Services General latency would exceed maximum\n- **Corrective Action:** Implement Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for critical services.\n- **Configuration Change:** Enable low latency mode and reduce processing delay.\n- **Risk Mitigation:** Monitor throughput degradation during latency optimization.\n- **Success Criteria:** Predicted URLLC services latency remains within the specified limit.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Step-by-Step Corrective Actions:\n\n1. Enable Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for critical services.\n2. Implement gradual energy optimization with continuous monitoring.\n3. Consider antenna-level power optimization instead of full BS power reduction.\n4. Monitor network performance during configuration changes.\n5. Implement phased latency optimizations before energy savings.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Configuration Changes to Meet Policy Requirements:\n\n- Enable low latency mode.\n- Reduce processing delay.\n- Implement gradual power reduction.\n- Consider antenna-level power optimization.\n- Utilize Nokia AirScale BaseFlow traffic steering.\n- Enable Nokia ReefShark beamforming optimization.\n- Utilize Nokia energy-aware load balancing.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Risk Mitigation Strategies:\n\n- Monitor throughput degradation during latency and energy optimizations.\n- Continuously monitor network performance during configuration changes.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Success Criteria for Each Healing Step:\n\n- Each corrective action should result in the specific parameter meeting the policy-defined maximum limit.\n- Network performance should be continuously monitored to ensure improvements without degradation.\n\n---\n\nThis detailed healing plan provides a systematic approach to address critical policy violations in the 5G network optimization, focusing on practical implementation for a 5G network engineer.\n\nIf you need further assistance or clarification on any specific aspect of the plan, feel free to ask.",
