ia:** Ensure predicted latency for URLLC services stays within 1.0ms.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Step-by-Step Corrective Actions:\n\n1. Enable low latency mode and reduce processing delay for critical services.\n2. Implement Nokia ultra-low latency algorithms for URLLC and autonomous vehicle network slices.\n3. Gradually reduce power while monitoring network slice latency and transmission quality.\n4. Consider antenna-level power optimization and load-based dynamic energy optimization.\n5. Continuously monitor throughput degradation during optimization processes.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Configuration Changes to Meet Policy Requirements:\n\n- Enable low latency mode and reduce processing delay.\n- Implement gradual power reduction and load-based dynamic energy optimization.\n- Consider antenna-level power optimization for transmission power control.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Risk Mitigation Strategies:\n\n- Monitor throughput degradation during latency and energy optimization.\n- Continuously monitor network slice latency and transmission quality.\n- Implement gradual changes to minimize impact on network performance.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Success Criteria for Each Healing Step:\n\n- Achieve latency optimization within specified limits for each service.\n- Ensure predicted values stay within policy-defined thresholds.\n- Maintain network performance while implementing configuration changes.\n\n---\n\nBy following this detailed healing plan, you can systematically address the critical policy violations in your 5G network optimization deployment. Focus on practical implementation and monitor the success criteria at each step to ensure compliance and improved network performance.",
