  "healing_plan": "Healing Plan: PLAN_1003_simu5g-e4f44d7b\nObjective\n- Resolve the critical policy violation where predicted DL throughput = 0.024 Mbps < demand-aware floor = 0.038 Mbps (80% of baseline), and restore compliance so optimization deployment can proceed.\n- Target a safe margin above the floor (recommend target DL throughput \u2265 0.05 Mbps per affected flow/UE class) while limiting negative side effects (energy, interference, user-impact).\n\nOverview & Immediate Actions\n- Violation severity: critical \u2014 blocks optimization until throughput meets policy floor.\n- Approach: fast diagnostics \u2192 short-term mitigation to reach floor \u2192 staged, low-risk tuning (vendor optimizations) \u2192 validate and finalize with continuous compliance monitoring and rollback guards.\n- Timescales: Diagnostic triage (0\u201330 min); Immediate mitigation (0.5\u20132 hours); Vendor/RAN tuning (2\u20138 hours); Monitoring & stabilization (24\u201372 hours).\n\nPre-checks (execute immediately)\n1. Confirm scope\n   - Identify affected cells/sectors, slice(s) and QoS/5QI classes where predicted DL throughput is below floor.\n   - Confirm baseline used to compute the 80% floor and timeframe for prediction (traffic model/time-of-day).\n2. Collect baseline KPIs (last 1\u20134 hours)\n   - Cell DL throughput, PRB utilization, DL PRB allocation per slice/QoS\n   - CQI distribution, MCS index distribution, BLER (transport + PHY), RLC retransmission rate\n   - RSRP/RSRQ per UE distribution, number of active UEs, throughput per UE\n   - Handover success/failure rates, ERAB drops, queue lengths, scheduler logs\n3. Confirm transport/backhaul and UPF health\n   - Check backhaul capacity, packet loss, latency, bufferbloat. If backhaul is saturated, fix before RAN changes.\n\nPhase 0 \u2014 Fast Diagnostic (30\u201360 min)\nActions:\n- Run targeted KPI queries for the affected cells for last 15\u201360 min.\n- Use drive/test UEs if necessary to validate predicted throughput